{
  "description": "TAI Julian Dates converted to TT and TDB, cross-checked against astropy. Each Julian Date is a two-part value [jd1, jd2] so the comparison stays below a nanosecond, where a single float would lose tens of microseconds. The cases are anchor dates, a deterministic sweep across the domain crossed with a palette of day fractions, and a sub-second stress at two dates.",
